; setline_index_beats_domain: the index is checked before the value.
;
; Both faults are available here -- index 10 is past a size-4 sample and 5 is
; outside {0, 1} -- so the vector pins which one a program sees. The index
; wins because a write that addresses no variable has no domain to be
; measured against: the domain is a property of the slot being written.
;
; This is the ordering that breaks if the domain check is hoisted above
; bounded_index, which is a natural thing to do when the value is already on
; the stack and the index still needs converting.

PUSH 4
BSMX r0          ; binary sample, size 4

PUSH 10          ; past the end
PUSH 5           ; and out of domain
SETLINE r0
HALT
